1
00:00:04,520 --> 00:00:09,680
This section walks us through initializing the repo client, which is basically the tool that manages

2
00:00:09,680 --> 00:00:12,360
all the git repositories needed to build Android.

3
00:00:13,280 --> 00:00:17,560
First step, we create a new working directory where all the source code will live.

4
00:00:18,440 --> 00:00:20,480
Keep in mind this thing's huge.

5
00:00:20,480 --> 00:00:24,320
It can take up over 300GB of space, so plan ahead.

6
00:00:25,240 --> 00:00:27,080
Then we run repo init.

7
00:00:27,960 --> 00:00:29,760
We are passing a few flags here.

8
00:00:30,600 --> 00:00:33,680
Partial clone helps reduce the initial download size.

9
00:00:34,560 --> 00:00:35,000
No use.

10
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:41,240
Superproject tells repo not to use the Superproject feature and b Android latest release means we want

11
00:00:41,240 --> 00:00:43,560
the latest official Android release branch.

12
00:00:44,480 --> 00:00:49,840
The U flag provides the URL for the manifest repo, which is like the blueprint of the source tree.

13
00:00:50,800 --> 00:00:56,080
Once that's done, we should see a confirmation that repo has been initialized in the current directory.

14
00:01:02,730 --> 00:01:07,010
Alright, now let's jump into the terminal and actually run these commands.

15
00:01:08,010 --> 00:01:12,490
First I'll create the working directory with mkdir and CD into it.

16
00:01:23,650 --> 00:01:27,370
Then I'll run the repo init command with all the required flags.

17
00:01:28,410 --> 00:01:31,490
This part usually takes a minute or two to set everything up.

18
00:01:32,490 --> 00:01:36,450
Once we get the message saying repo has been initialized, we are good to go.

19
00:01:45,170 --> 00:01:45,690
Down.

20
00:01:47,250 --> 00:01:48,930
Up down.

21
00:01:51,130 --> 00:01:52,330
Up up up.

22
00:01:55,490 --> 00:01:56,330
Up.

23
00:01:57,490 --> 00:01:57,970
Repo.

24
00:01:58,010 --> 00:01:59,930
Initialization is now complete.

25
00:02:04,770 --> 00:02:06,210
Next up is repo sink.

26
00:02:07,210 --> 00:02:12,970
The C flag makes sure we only pull the current branch, and J8 speeds things up by using eight parallel

27
00:02:12,970 --> 00:02:13,530
threads.

28
00:02:14,490 --> 00:02:15,450
Now heads up.

29
00:02:15,450 --> 00:02:20,690
This sink can take over an hour depending on your internet speed and storage, so maybe go grab a coffee

30
00:02:20,730 --> 00:02:21,770
while it's working.

31
00:02:22,810 --> 00:02:26,410
Once it's done, we'll have the full Android source tree ready to build.

32
00:02:27,210 --> 00:02:28,170
Let's do it!

33
00:03:05,940 --> 00:03:06,260
Up.

34
00:03:09,860 --> 00:03:11,100
Up up up.

35
00:03:14,220 --> 00:03:15,220
Up up.

36
00:03:15,220 --> 00:03:15,500
Up.

37
00:03:17,700 --> 00:03:18,460
Up.

38
00:03:21,100 --> 00:03:22,900
Up up up up.

39
00:03:24,340 --> 00:03:28,820
During the repo sync, I encountered some issues caused by network instability.

40
00:03:29,740 --> 00:03:36,060
To work around this, I had to sync the repo using a single process repo sync with J1.

41
00:04:07,780 --> 00:04:09,540
The repo sync was successful.

42
00:04:10,540 --> 00:04:15,300
As I mentioned earlier, I encountered a network latency issue during the process.

43
00:04:16,180 --> 00:04:21,580
If you face a similar problem, try syncing the repo using a single process to avoid such issues.

44
00:04:22,580 --> 00:04:24,420
Now let's launch the lunch menu.

45
00:04:28,220 --> 00:04:29,540
We have one issue here.

46
00:04:30,460 --> 00:04:32,980
This happens starting Android 14 builds.

47
00:04:33,900 --> 00:04:36,100
The system fails to show the lunch menu.

48
00:04:37,100 --> 00:04:38,620
There is a solution to this.

49
00:04:52,820 --> 00:04:56,670
If you try using the lunch directly like this, it's not going to work.

50
00:04:57,710 --> 00:05:00,110
I found this solution in XDA forums.

51
00:05:01,030 --> 00:05:06,630
First, export the target underscore release variable by running export target underscore release equals

52
00:05:06,670 --> 00:05:07,470
AP tour.

53
00:05:08,470 --> 00:05:12,590
Next run the command build underscore build underscore underscore cache.

54
00:05:13,670 --> 00:05:16,870
After this run launch and you will be able see the lunch menu.

55
00:05:24,550 --> 00:05:26,750
Let's go ahead and build the emulator.

56
00:05:27,630 --> 00:05:30,070
I am choosing automotive build in this case.

57
00:05:30,990 --> 00:05:34,150
If you need phone build please select the build accordingly.

58
00:06:02,640 --> 00:06:03,000
I.

59
00:08:48,410 --> 00:08:50,890
The build was successful without any issues.

60
00:08:51,930 --> 00:08:54,250
Sorry I missed to take video capture of it.

61
00:08:55,090 --> 00:08:56,850
Now let's start the emulator.

62
00:08:57,730 --> 00:09:03,530
The settings app is already open since I tried opening the emulator earlier before capturing this video.

63
00:09:04,490 --> 00:09:06,610
In your case, you should see the launcher.

64
00:09:34,930 --> 00:09:35,610
Thank you.

65
00:09:36,650 --> 00:09:38,090
That's all for this video.

66
00:09:39,010 --> 00:09:43,690
Please give it a try on your end and feel free to reach out if you run into any issues.

67
00:09:44,610 --> 00:09:46,410
I hope this session was helpful.

